[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3767141161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114#issuecomment-3767141161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115114","id":3767141161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gigMp","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T08:48:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T08:48:04Z","body":"Hello, thank you for your work! I feel like we can also change the behaviour of SDL to make the existing code work with Switch controllers, it doesn't look too hard to fix, see also:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_switch.c#L1617-L1628\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_switch.c#L734-L753\r\nMaybe we can make the Switch driver report having a `SDL_PROP_JOYSTICK_CAP_MONO_LED_BOOLEAN` capability, similarly to how PS4 controllers work:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapi_ps4.c#L891-L906\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/741fb8a30687d0662ab6b5c04a2a531440dd29d9/thirdparty/sdl/joystick/hidapi/SDL_hidapijoystick.c#L802-L816\r\n\r\nWhat do you think? :)\r\nShould we also ask the SDL developers what they think about it?\r\n\r\nAnother reason I suggest doing this inside SDL is because the current approach of changing the hint will (probably) modify the home LED of all connected Switch controllers, not just one that was used for `set_joy_light`, so it might feel like a bug.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3767141161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770607474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114#issuecomment-3770607474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115114","id":3770607474,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gvudy","user":{"login":"ThiLelito","id":125714191,"node_id":"U_kgDOB34_Dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125714191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito","html_url":"https://github.com/ThiLelito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T01:11:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T01:11:22Z","body":"Hey, thanks for your response!\r\n\r\n> Maybe we can make the Switch driver report having a `SDL_PROP_JOYSTICK_CAP_MONO_LED_BOOLEAN` capability, similarly to how PS4 controllers work.\r\n> Should we also ask the SDL developers what they think about it?\r\n\r\nI think that we could, it seems to be the best option now that you mentioned it.\r\nI guess we should ask the developers aswell, as they are the ones mostly responsible for the SDL. They may have a better idea of how we can overcome this :)\r\n\r\n> Another reason I suggest doing this inside SDL is because the current approach of changing the hint will (probably) modify the home LED of all connected Switch controllers, not just one that was used for `set_joy_light`, so it might feel like a bug.\r\n\r\nNow that you've mentioned it, yes, I can't really test it since I don't have two or more controllers with this capability but as the hint is changed without providing the joypad/gamepad, it probably changes every controllers LED lights.\r\n\r\nAlso thanks @AThousandShips for the suggested change, it really is better.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770607474/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788099227","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114#issuecomment-3788099227","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115114","id":3788099227,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hyc6b","user":{"login":"ThiLelito","id":125714191,"node_id":"U_kgDOB34_Dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125714191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito","html_url":"https://github.com/ThiLelito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T04:11:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T04:13:11Z","body":"As discussed and suggested by @Nintorch , I tried changing the Switch SDL file and it seems to work properly, I just can't test it on multiple controllers but it may work as intended now.\r\n\r\n- I've removed the code previously added to `joypad.sdl` since they are not necessary anymore\r\n- Done the implementation in `SDL_hidapi_switch.c` as discussed and it seems to work as intended. The only logical difference is that now it should work for independent controllers as it is now treated as a property instead of a hint.\r\n- It should work to both the Pro Controller and the Right Joy-Con (I confess I am not sure of how the Joy-con Pair is detected, but as the Pair includes the Right Joy-con I've added it aswell)\r\n\r\n_I should note that from my tests, the Pro Controller Home LED has different levels of brightness instead of a continuous range. It isn't an issue but I feel like this should be known._","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788099227/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788234676","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114#issuecomment-3788234676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115114","id":3788234676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hy9-0","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T04:57:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T04:57:31Z","body":"Looks good to me! May I ask if the code works if you connect both the Pro Controller and the right Joy Con and call `set_joy_light()` on one of them?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788234676/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788361720","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115114#issuecomment-3788361720","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115114","id":3788361720,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7hzc_4","user":{"login":"ThiLelito","id":125714191,"node_id":"U_kgDOB34_Dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/125714191?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito","html_url":"https://github.com/ThiLelito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThiLelito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T05:29:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T05:33:01Z","body":"AFAIK it should work as both Pro Controllers and Joy Cons use the same base file (`SDL_hidapi_switch`) and I've added them to the `HIDAPI_DriverSwitch_GetJoystickCapabilities` so they should work equally (and separately). Sadly I can't confirm 100% that it works since I can't test it as I only have the NS2 Joy Cons* (and a NS1 Pro Controller)\r\n\r\n_* The NS2 Joy Cons and NS2 Pro Controllers don't have this LED so they wouldn't work whatsoever._","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788361720/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3788415206","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pu